# FASM feature literals and fragments extracted from VTR's FASM writer test
# suite (`utils/fasm/test/test_fasm.cpp`) and its test architecture file
# (`utils/fasm/test/test_fasm_arch.xml`). See `tests/corpus/vtr/README.md`
# for provenance (repo, commit, licence) and `docs/rewrite/TASKS.md` T1.5
# (this corpus is used by `tools/difftest.py`, not by VTR itself: VTR keeps
# no committed `.fasm` files, only C++ tests and `fasm_*` architecture
# metadata that its `FasmWriterVisitor` turns into FASM lines at runtime).
#
# Every line below is independently valid per the FASM grammar
# (`docs/specification/syntax.rst`); most are fragments (feature name
# components VTR's fasm writer would compose into a longer dotted feature,
# or the raw text of a `fasm_features`/`fasm_lut` architecture metadata
# attribute) rather than full hierarchical feature paths, since
# `test_fasm.cpp`'s own checks are substring/regex matches
# (`StartsWith`/`ContainsSubstring`), not full literal FASM lines, and the
# architecture's `fasm_prefix`/`fasm_mux` metadata is written with `{tag}`
# placeholders that VTR fills in at runtime from each tile's
# `fasm_placeholders` metadata (see below).

# --- Literal string asserted equal in a unit test ---------------------
# test_fasm.cpp, TEST_CASE("substitute_tags_correct"): the feature
# "{prefix}CLB_{loc}_{site}" with tags {prefix: "L", loc: "X7Y8",
# site: "SLICE"} substitutes to exactly this (REQUIRE(result ==
# "LCLB_X7Y8_SLICE")). A feature name with no address or value, valid FASM
# on its own.
LCLB_X7Y8_SLICE

# --- fasm_features metadata (test_fasm_arch.xml), verbatim ------------
# <mode name="n2_lut5"> ... <meta name="fasm_features">: no placeholders,
# used verbatim by VTR when that mode is selected.
N2_LUT5
# <mode name="n1_lut6"> ... <meta name="fasm_features">.
N1_LUT6

# --- fasm_lut metadata (test_fasm_arch.xml), verbatim ------------------
# <pb_type name="lut5" ...> (inside mode n2_lut5) <meta name="fasm_lut">:
# the bit-array feature+address VTR writes the LUT truth table into (no
# `=`: a bare `Feature FeatureAddress` is valid FASM per the grammar, it is
# VTR's own writer that appends ` = <value>` when it emits this).
LUT[31:0]
# <pb_type name="lut6" ...> (inside mode n1_lut6) <meta name="fasm_lut">.
LUT6[63:0]

# --- fasm_mux metadata, mux1 (OUT_MUX) in both lut5/lut6 modes ----------
# <mux name="mux1" ...><meta name="fasm_mux">: "ff.Q : OUT_MUX.FFQ" (the
# part after ":" is the FASM feature fragment written when input "ff.Q" is
# selected); no placeholders.
OUT_MUX.FFQ
# Same <meta name="fasm_mux">, other line: "lut5.out : OUT_MUX.LUT,DISABLE_FF"
# -- VTR splits a comma separated value into several features enabled
# together; each half on its own line here.
OUT_MUX.LUT
DISABLE_FF

# --- fasm_mux metadata, direct1 in mode n1_lut6 (ble6.in -> lut6.in) ----
# <direct name="direct1" ...><meta name="fasm_mux">: six "ble6.in[N] : INN"
# lines, no placeholders (this fasm_mux selects one of 6 LUT input pins by
# a plain feature name).
IN0
IN1
IN2
IN3
IN4
IN5

# --- fasm_prefix / fasm_placeholders metadata, placeholders substituted -
# The architecture's per-tile <meta name="fasm_placeholders"> (in
# <layout>/<fixed_layout>) defines LOC/LR/SING for each (x,y) instance;
# VTR's fasm::substitute_tags (exercised directly by the unit test above)
# fills them into every "{tag}"-containing fasm_prefix/fasm_mux string for
# that tile instance. "SING=NULL" means substitute the empty string (see
# fasm.cpp: "When the value is NULL then substitute empty string"), not
# the literal text "NULL" (utils/fasm/src/fasm.cpp, substitute_tags).
#
# Tile (x=1,y=1): fasm_placeholders LOC=X1Y1, LR=L, SING=_SING;
# fasm_prefix=CLB.
#
# <pb_type name="ff" ...><meta name="fasm_prefix">ALUT_{LR}</meta>
# (mode n1_lut6) substituted with LR=L:
ALUT_L
# <pb_type name="fle" ...><meta name="fasm_prefix">
#   FLE0{SING}_{LOC} FLE1{SING}_{LOC}
# </meta> (two space separated prefixes, one per `fle` sub-block, num_pb=2)
# substituted with SING=_SING, LOC=X1Y1:
FLE0_SING_X1Y1
FLE1_SING_X1Y1
# <mux name="mux_fle0_in0" ...><meta name="fasm_mux">: first entry
# "clb.I[0] : FLE0{SING}_{LOC}.IN0_XBAR_I0" substituted the same way.
FLE0_SING_X1Y1.IN0_XBAR_I0

# Tile (x=2,y=2): fasm_placeholders LOC=X2Y2, LR=R, SING=NULL (empty);
# fasm_prefix=PLB.
#
# ALUT_{LR} substituted with LR=R:
ALUT_R
# FLE0{SING}_{LOC} FLE1{SING}_{LOC} substituted with SING="" (NULL), LOC=X2Y2:
FLE0_X2Y2
FLE1_X2Y2
# mux_fle0_in0's "clb.I[0] : FLE0{SING}_{LOC}.IN0_XBAR_I0" substituted the
# same way.
FLE0_X2Y2.IN0_XBAR_I0
